            "review_title": "Review at AT Hanoi",
            "review_text": "Danielle S\n33 contributions\n0\nGreat food, Outstanding Service\nNov 2015\nDuring our first trip to Hanoi, we stayed right across from this restaurant, which was lucky for us. This is also the first place we went to eat when we came back to Hanoi. The food here is good and reasonably priced (for a sit down place. Of course you are going to find cheaper food on the street). They have really good pizza, a cast iron skillet rice dish that is savory and rich, and probably the best special fried rice I've ever had. Ever. \n\nI keep saying this about places in Vietnam (the friendliest place I have visited in SE Asia so far) but it is really the people that make the place. The service is good - almost Western style as they check on you a lot which isn't typical. The best is Mai. She has the most welcoming attitude and smile. She also is very fluent in English, and she likes to talk to her customers. You feel more like an old friend than a customer even on your first visit. The owner is lovely as well. She had me hand write a review of their pizza because I liked it so much and then had my friend face-time her husband because she was so excited by our review. \n\nIf you are looking for good food and good prices without a giant crowd, this place is where you should be.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten November 14, 2015",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-15",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
